('new-home-drinking-water-checklist-gujar-khan',
'Moving Into a New Home in Gujar Khan? A Drinking Water Checklist',
'A practical move-in checklist for sorting reliable drinking water in your new home, from your first bottle to a settled weekly routine, without the stress.',
'<p>Sorting drinking water is one of the easiest things to overlook when you move house and one of the first things you miss when it is not there. This checklist gets a new home in Gujar Khan, Rawat, Kallar Syedan or anywhere across our coverage area set up with reliable drinking water quickly, so the kettle, the cooking and the cold glass at the end of a long day are all covered from day one.</p>

<h2>Before you move: two quick decisions</h2>
<h3>1. Decide how you will drink and store water</h3>
<p>Most homes settle on a <a href="/product/water-dispenser">hot and cold dispenser</a> fed by <a href="/product/19-litre-refill-bottle">19 litre bottles</a>. It covers chilled drinking water in summer and hot water for tea in winter, from one unit. Decide whether you will buy the dispenser for Rs 42,000 or rent it for Rs 2,000 per month, a choice we break down in our <a href="/blog/water-dispenser-buy-or-rent-guide">buy or rent guide</a>.</p>
<h3>2. Check you are inside the delivery area</h3>
<p>Pak-Everests delivers free across Gujar Khan, Mandra, Daultala, Bewal, Habib Chowk, Kallar Syedan, Rawat, Adiala Road, DHA Islamabad, Bahria Town Rawalpindi and the wider Rawalpindi and Islamabad market. You can see the full list on our <a href="/coverage-areas">coverage areas page</a>. If you are near the edge, just ask.</p>

<h2>Move-in day: get water in the house first</h2>
<p>On the day itself, an early delivery means you are not hunting for a shop while surrounded by boxes. Place your first <a href="/order">order online</a> or on WhatsApp a day or two ahead and ask for move-in day delivery. Start with one dispenser and two bottles, one in use and one spare, which is the right setup for most families.</p>

<h2>The first week: find your rhythm</h2>
<p>Over the first week, note how many days your first bottle lasts. That single number tells you your household use and sets your whole routine. Remember that summer use in the Potohar region can be double winter use, so if you move in the cooler months, expect to order more often once the heat arrives.</p>

<h2>Settle into a simple routine</h2>
<p>Once you know your usage, set a standing schedule so refills arrive before you run dry. The households that never run out keep one spare bottle on rotation and order the moment the spare goes into use, not when the last drop is gone. Because delivery is free, ordering a day early never costs anything.</p>

<h2>Renting your home rather than owning it?</h2>
<p>If you are renting the property, lean towards renting the <a href="/product/water-dispenser">dispenser</a> too, at Rs 2,000 per month with servicing included, rather than buying one at Rs 42,000. It keeps your upfront costs low during a move, avoids carrying a machine if you relocate again, and hands maintenance to us. If you later settle somewhere long term, buying becomes the cheaper choice, and switching from renting to buying is straightforward. Owners of the home they are moving into usually do the opposite and buy from the start, since they know they will use it for years. Our <a href="/blog/water-dispenser-buy-or-rent-guide">buy or rent guide</a> works through the exact break even point if you want the numbers.</p>

<h2>A note for families with young children</h2>
<p>Homes with babies and young children should treat drinking water as a first day priority, not an afterthought. Children are more sensitive to waterborne germs than adults, and feeds, formula and constant small drinks all depend on a safe supply. Having a licensed, re-mineralised source in the house from move-in day removes one real worry during an already stressful time. Keep the dispenser tap clean, store bottles shaded and off the floor, and you have a reliable supply for the whole family from the moment you arrive.</p>

<h2>A complete move-in checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>Choose a dispenser and decide buy or rent.</li>
<li>Confirm your address is in the <a href="/coverage-areas">coverage area</a>.</li>
<li>Order your first dispenser and two bottles for move-in day.</li>
<li>Note how many days the first bottle lasts.</li>
<li>Set a standing delivery based on that number.</li>
<li>Keep one spare bottle on rotation at all times.</li>
<li>Store bottles cool and shaded, off the bare floor.</li>
<li>Save our WhatsApp numbers for quick reorders.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Do not forget the water for tea, cooking and guests</h2>
<p>It is easy to plan only for drinking and forget how much water a home really uses. In a Pakistani household, tea alone can account for several cups of water a day, and cooking, washing vegetables for salad, and making feeds for young children all add up. Guests increase it further, and in this region guests arrive often and without much notice. When you set your first routine, base it on real household use rather than drinking alone, and keep a spare bottle in hand precisely so an unexpected visit or a busy cooking day never leaves you short. It is far more pleasant to have water ready than to apologise to guests over an empty dispenser.</p>

<h2>Saving our numbers for quick reorders</h2>
<p>One small step makes the whole routine easier: save our WhatsApp numbers, 0333 5592206 and 0332 2901309, in your phone on move-in day. Reordering then takes seconds, a quick message rather than a search each time. Households that keep the number handy reorder promptly when the spare goes on, which is exactly the habit that prevents ever running dry. It is a tiny thing that quietly keeps the water flowing.</p>

<h2>Why families choose a local licensed plant</h2>
<p>When you are new to an area, it is hard to know which supplier to trust. The safe default is a <strong>Punjab Food Authority</strong> approved plant that will show you its process and puts a batch code on every bottle. Pak-Everests runs a full <a href="/purification-process">eight stage purification process</a> with re-mineralisation for balanced taste, and being based in the Potohar region means your new home is well inside a reliable, short delivery route rather than at the end of a fragile one.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>How fast can I get my first delivery?</h3>
<p>Order a day ahead and we will usually have you covered for move-in day. Message 0333 5592206 on WhatsApp for the quickest response.</p>
<h3>What if I use more water than I expected?</h3>
<p>Just adjust your standing order. There is no penalty for changing quantity or frequency, and free delivery means ordering more often costs nothing extra.</p>
<p>Starting fresh in a new home? <a href="/order">Place your first order</a> or message us on WhatsApp, and we will have safe water waiting when you arrive.</p>',
